      "comment": "SOUTHAMPTON FLARE (5) gets the nod off a strong late fourth at this track, where he was beaten three lengths after settling well back and charging home from an awkward position. He has two wins from three starts at 1100m and has already shown he is effective at this venue. Key runner. BOLD SUITOR (3) is the danger resuming for the Gary Clarke stable. His Moe failure on heavy ground came after he was slow away as a well-supported favourite, while the Bendigo BM62 sixth prior was much sounder. In the mix for the new yard. TIGERS ROAR (2) was run down only late first-up, beaten a long neck, and has proven track-and-trip form. Include. ANKLE ROLEX (1) is back from a five-month break with strong prior form at this venue. Proven at the trip and can give this a shake.",
